# Auxiliaries for the final contradiction in Higman (1963), Lemma 3

For a `ξ`-abelian-normal subgroup `A` of a Suzuki 2-group and an element `u`, put
`φ_u(a) = a · (u⁻¹ a u)`.  This is the "norm" map `1 + conjᵤ`; on an abelian `A` it is an
endomorphism, and it plays the central role in the last step of Higman's Lemma 3: the group
generated by its values is a `ξ`-invariant subgroup of `A`, hence a power subgroup `A ^ (2 ^ j)`,
whereas the group `⟨φ_u(A), u²⟩` is generated over it by the single element `u²`.

The file collects the elementary group-theoretic facts about `phiVal`, `phiA` (the subgroup
generated by the values of `φ_u`) and `Bsub = ⟨φ_u(A), u²⟩`, together with the `ξ`-invariance
of these subgroups.
-/

import Mathlib
import Submission.Work.Higman.Defs
import Submission.Work.Higman.Basic
import Submission.Work.Higman.PowSub
import Submission.Work.Higman.SuzukiMaximal
import Submission.Work.Higman.homogeneous_structure

